comments[30]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T03:24:21.600Z",codex-agent,"Deferred scope: resolve an ancestor change and automatically rebase all descendants while preserving stable change ids, file identities, unrelated edits and unresolved alternatives. Include repeated and overlapping disagreements in conflict-aware replay, across sibling branches and tags. The first slice resolves at HEAD only and does not claim propagation."
  "2026-10-18T18:18:22.654Z",codex-agent,"Plan: extend resolve with --at for an explicit ancestor and automatically select the originating conflict change when its units are inherited at HEAD. Replay all reachable branch/tag descendants with durable conflicts, stable change identities and one undoable ref transaction. Preserve descendant edits as new disagreements with their own projection. Verify concurrent resolutions in linked worktrees and a real three-author PM tracker. Release policy and dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T18:19:29.081Z",codex-agent,"Selection decision: preserve the established default resolving change at HEAD; add --at <change> for an explicit conflicted ancestor. The earlier automatic-origin idea is superseded so resolving a descendant does not unexpectedly rewrite older work. --at selects the original change, inserts a resolving change, and rebases its descendants across refs in one operation."
  "2026-10-18T18:28:02.864Z",codex-agent,"Current real tracker linked regression passed 8/8 with zero failures/skips/cancellations. Covers sibling branches/tags, detached HEAD, one-operation undo, field/text descendant edits, competing explicit choices (including metadata-only ours), partial fields, non-first-parent replay, structural refusal and three PM_AUTHOR tracker reads. Behavioral revert proofs in an isolated source copy: remove only descendant replay from repointDescendant -> node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^ancestor resolution\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fails 0/1 (ours instead of theirs); remove only the competingResolutions merge block -> node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^concurrent resolutions in independent\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fails 0/1 (theirs silently overwrites ours). Production TypeScript is imported directly; no dist rebuild needed for these proofs. Live source remains restored. Full release gates and pushed-head CI follow. Linked result tracking is disabled by existing project policy."
  "2026-10-18T18:41:21.766Z",codex-agent,"The merged conflict-storage regression rerun passed 49/49 with zero failures/skips/cancellations. First pushed-head CI and the first local release run correctly rejected a duplicate worktree import; commit 9c73343 combines the import and regenerates the staged-source archive. Added stable change-id selectors: a unique reachable version resolves, detached HEAD participates, and multiple live versions refuse with ambiguous_change instead of selecting arbitrarily. The next full release checks run from the next committed source; the interrupted prior run is excluded from acceptance."
  "2026-10-18T18:45:16.918Z",codex-agent,"Expanded concurrent-resolution acceptance covers equal choices plus independent edits within the same record/text payload, absent fields, EOF-only choices, and choices already recorded as ordinary content conflicts. Focused propagation suite passed 12/12 before the final duplicate-unit scenario; the new scenario checks both all-units and one-unit disagreements. Removed only impossible correlated-type/default branches from the helper, retaining typed conflict alternatives. Current source is entering both complete isolated release gates; earlier interrupted or old-head runs are not acceptance."
  "2026-10-18T18:47:03.610Z",codex-agent,"CI on 9c73343 passed all functional tests but correctly refused uncovered branches in the new helper, text-field refusal and descendant replay. Added real mode-change replay refusal (the earlier deleted-path test refused earlier at path visibility), a merge descendant with one unchanged parent outside the rewritten ancestry, equal/absent/EOF choices and one-vs-two-unit resolution conflicts. The two new CI boundary scenarios pass 2/2. No thresholds or workflows change; complete npm/Bun gates restart on this committed source."
  "2026-10-18T18:52:17.580Z",codex-agent,"Final identity regression found an inherited-conflict rename was refused by a path-only visibility check. Resolution now recognizes the visible stable FileId and aligns the affected parent identity to the descendant path before replaying value deltas. Real rename plus later-descendant proof passes; deletion in a sibling and rename onto a different parent identity both refuse atomically, 3/3 total. Existing FileIds and change IDs are asserted unchanged. Unsupported structural transitions remain explicit refusals. The obsolete source gate runs were stopped; both complete release gates restart after this commit."
  "2026-10-18T19:07:00.877Z",codex-agent,"Shifted text regression confirmed two independent faults: current-base stable anchors were skipped by diff3, and conflict inheritance compared shifted object addresses directly. Fixed the anchor scan and mapped origin-matching units into each side before deciding whether a resolution removed them. Current focused propagation suite passes 19/19; merge/rewrite module acceptance passes 95/95, including the propagation suite, with all new conflict-origin helper branches covered. Independent controlled reverts of the anchor and inheritance changes each make node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^shifted inherited text\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fail 0/1; a separate identity-alignment-only revert fails the renamed-inheritance test 0/1. Live source is restored. Full npm/Bun gates restart on the next committed source."
  "2026-10-18T19:31:41.704Z",codex-agent,"CI on cda435c measured all changed runtime files at 100% except one wildcard error-message branch in Repository.resolveConflicts. Added the explicit already-clean path refusal without --field. Its only functional failure was an old diff3 fixture that labelled first-two-line reordering and a fourth-line edit as overlapping; those edits are independent. The corrected fixture asserts a clean combined result and separately tests a real edit/move overlap with one complete marker group and preserved tail. These controls pass 3/3 with the legacy-mode control. Also reproduced legacy-mode silent loss of an unchanged-ours resolution: legacy merge now raises typed resolution_conflict before refs/index/bytes/operations change; recorded mode stores one dispute. Both field/text controls pass. Remove only that publication guard in an isolated source copy -> node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^legacy merge modes\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fails 0/1. No thresholds, dependency pins or workflows change."
  "2026-10-18T21:20:55.443Z",codex-agent,"Final source acceptance on 293444f4d9b2fc02e5b0062799ff108ed35504e0: unchanged npm run release:check AND bun run release:check pass with fresh HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 in independent full-history checkouts. Each coverage suite passes 1632/1632 tests, zero failures, skipped, cancelled or TODO; c8 --all --100 --per-file measures all 66 production files at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines: 23122/23122 statements and lines, 7093/7093 branches and 785/785 functions. ESLint reports no warnings; jscpd reports 0 clone pairs and 0% duplicated lines; docstrings cover 66 files and 364 declarations. Native TOON, stat-cache, committed self-host, production audit, identity audit, pack, changelog and release-attestation checks pass. Pushed-source CI passes Node 22/26, Windows launchers and CodeQL. Linked pm test pm-vcs-p7resolve --run --progress passes all 20 acceptance tests, including the real three-PM_AUTHOR tracker proof: both agents commit two descendants, the third resolves the ancestor, all four descendant snapshots keep stable IDs and read the chosen value, both refreshed working trees pass verify and plain pm list/get reads every item."
  "2026-10-18T21:21:06.033Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert receipts against the final source, using an isolated source copy and production TypeScript imports: (1) revert only descendant replay in repointDescendant; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^ancestor resolution carries through\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fails 0/1. (2) remove only competing-resolution detection; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^concurrent resolutions in independent\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fails 0/1. (3) remove only descendant FileId/path alignment; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^ancestor resolution follows a renamed\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fails 0/1. (4) restore only the old stable-anchor scan; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^shifted inherited text\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fails 0/1. (5) restore only raw-address conflict inheritance; the same shifted-text command fails 0/1. (6) remove only the legacy competing-choice refusal; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^legacy merge modes\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts fails 0/1. Each control has one failure, zero passes, skips or cancellations. Restored implementation passes 20/20 through the linked runner."
  "2026-10-18T21:21:12.445Z",codex-agent,"Handoff: structural replay disagreements still refuse atomically; signing and bisect remain separate Phase 7 items, and annotation is the independent PR #126. Release workflows and dependency pins are unchanged; publishing remains disabled pending owner approval. No new pm CLI/SDK defect was encountered. Existing linked-test result tracking is disabled by project policy, so comments retain the receipts. The item remains in_progress and is not closed; claim is released for review. Receipt-only changes will regenerate the committed self-host bundle after explicit staging; final CI and fresh-clone strict health will be checked at the receipt head before handoff."
  "2026-10-18T22:06:08.704Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: rechecked clean branch and open PR #125. Investigating the three unresolved review findings: unreachable ancestor publication, structural merge handling and duplicate conflict addresses. Will record behavioral regressions and narrow revert proofs before rerunning both release gates. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-10-18T22:08:24.136Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: all three findings confirmed and fixed. PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6tu_VV: engine/repo.ts refuses unreachable ancestor plans with unreachable_revision before refs/index/files/oplog publication. PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6tu_Vk: engine/rewrite.ts skips explicit-resolution inspection on unrecorded structural conflicts and unions fresh field conflicts with competing-resolution fields. PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6tu_Vp: final explicit conflict addresses are deduplicated when shifted inherited hunks converge. Four focused tests in test/resolution-propagation.test.ts pass; each corresponding fix was reverted alone and its selected test exited 1 (missing typed refusal; object_type_mismatch; omitted independent field; invalid_tree_entry for duplicate addresses). Restored all fixes. No finding refused; no review thread replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-18T22:51:05.651Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 complete on source 1a5a33703318001e47e1b1746e98c6e8f4128844. npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0 under fresh HOME with global/system Git identity disabled in independent full-history checkouts. Each: 1636/1636 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODO; c8 --all --100 --per-file: 66 production files, 23125 statements/lines, 785 functions, all 100%; branch totals are 7097 for npm and 7100 for Bun, both fully covered. ESLint zero warnings; jscpd zero clone pairs/0%; docstrings 66 files/364 declarations; native TOON, stat-cache, committed self-host, production/identity audits, pack, changelog and attestation checks pass. Exact-head CI run 39170996007 passes Linux Node 22/26 and Windows launchers; CodeQL also passes. Linked pm test runner passes 24/24; result tracking remains disabled by existing policy, so receipts are recorded here. Findings: unreachable_revision guard engine/repo.ts:2099; structural inspection guard engine/rewrite.ts:376 and complete field report :383; unique addresses :382. Four narrow controls each exit 1 with 0 pass/1 fail: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"PATTERN\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts, with PATTERN set separately to unreachable conflict, payload kind transition, both fresh and converging carried, reverting only its corresponding fix each time. No finding refused; no thread replies/resolutions. Final receipt commit changes only tracker/history and self-host archive; runtime/test/docs/workflows remain identical to the gated source. Item stays in_progress; releases remain disabled."
  "2026-10-19T01:59:55.627Z",codex-agent,"Integration after annotation PR #126 merged: normal-environment merge of origin/main into the resolve branch. The worktree was clean and clone-local receipt inventory was empty. Conflicts are limited to shared architecture/roadmap documentation and the generated self-host bundle; production Repository and command registration merged automatically. Keep both slices documented, take main changelog before regeneration, add a real resolved-unit annotation regression, check merge receipts and clean-clone health, then rerun unchanged isolated npm/Bun release gates. No review thread writes or release changes."
  "2026-10-19T02:02:43.020Z",codex-agent,"Interaction regression: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^resolved units annotate\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts passes 1/1. A real temporary repository exercises field and text disputes, ours/theirs/base choices, the inserted resolving change and a replayed descendant; stable descendant IDs, unrelated origins and verify are checked. The unchanged ours projection previously retained its pre-resolution setter. Annotation now excludes cleared disputed units from unchanged-parent inheritance. In an isolated source copy, restoring only the pre-integration annotation implementation while retaining the new test fails 0/1 (exit 1), on item.toon take ours attribution; candidate passes 1/1. Production TypeScript is imported directly, with no SDK mocks. Build:test, lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass. Normal-environment merge inventory remains empty and health reports no merge_receipts_pending, so no reconcile was run. Local strict health flags an ignored extension host-version skew against the unchanged pinned CLI; committed-head health will be proved independently in a fresh clone with a compatible project extension."
  "2026-10-19T02:09:00.842Z",codex-agent,"Merge source afb8a12ffa450ad8dfb41ac69a20f43f122e4bdf combines the previous resolve head with main 24f6a937d0844a6d55ebdc19785d37e821c9f2ad (merged annotation PR #126). Shared architecture and README retain both delivered slice contracts; main CHANGELOG was selected and regenerated. The self-host bundle was regenerated after staging and committed with the merge; HEAD accept:self-host and changelog:check pass. Linked resolve acceptance passes 25/25 and annotation passes 23/23. Fresh no-local clone strict health with merge drivers required passes, with no merge receipts pending; existing non-blocking telemetry, stale-item and historical provenance advisories remain. Both full release gates now run on this exact committed source in independent full-history clones with fresh HOME and global/system Git identity disabled. Final receipts will record gate counts; no release or review-thread actions."
  "2026-10-19T02:10:34.169Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator added two review findings before the combined push: unique conflict-origin fallback when staged coordinate mappings compose differently, and virtual-base handling of competing resolutions. The merge is already committed at afb8a12; no second merge was started. Read both complete threads. The earlier npm/Bun gate runs on the pre-fix source were deliberately stopped as superseded, not counted as completed or failing certification. Add real-history regressions and independent narrow revert controls for both fixes, then run both complete release gates on the updated exact source and push once. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-10-19T02:14:07.080Z",codex-agent,"Both new findings are confirmed and fixed. PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6tw6pG: inheritedConflict prefers an exact mapped address, then accepts a sole origin-key candidate; multiple unmatched candidates remain ambiguous. The real staged-edit/branch-merge regression reproduces the former silent loss of the unresolved unit and checks original alternatives plus verify. Narrow control restoring only inheritedConflict to afb8a12 fails node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^sequentially carried\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts, 0/1, exit 1: conflict count disappears. PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6tw6pN: RewriteContext marks heuristic virtual-base construction; Repository passes it only there, so competing-resolution checks remain active for ordinary merges. A real criss-cross reconciliation history covers field and text choices; the outer recorded merge retains disputes and verify passes. Restoring only the changed virtual-base functions to afb8a12 fails node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^criss-crossed resolution\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts, 0/1, exit 1, resolution_conflict. Independent candidate controls plus the resolve/annotate interaction pass 3/3. Ordinary legacy refusal regression also passes. Build:test, lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass; production coverage inventory and thresholds are unchanged. No SDK mocks or thread mutations."
  "2026-10-19T03:08:02.089Z",codex-agent,"Complete exact-source certification at 7abf65e07fc93987ef49336ae2b7b674d246a4c5: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0 in independent full-history clones with fresh HOME and global/system Git identity disabled. Each passed 1662/1662 tests, zero failed/skipped/cancelled/TODO. c8 all/per-file coverage is 100% in every dimension across 67 production files: 23453 statements/lines, 7348 branches, 804 functions for each runtime. ESLint has zero warnings, jscpd has zero clone pairs/0%, and docstrings cover 67 files/365 declarations. Native TOON, real installed stat-cache strace, committed self-host, production/identity audits, pack, changelog, release-date and publish-attestation checks pass. Linked resolve suite is 27/27; both new review regressions and the resolve-to-annotate interaction passed inside both full gates. Narrow independent revert failures are recorded above. No clone-local merge receipts exist and no reconciliation was needed. The pre-fix gate runs were deliberately superseded when the orchestrator added the findings, never counted as completed certification. This validation record and claim release will be committed with a regenerated staged-source self-host bundle; runtime/tests/docs/dependencies/workflows remain identical to the gated source. Final HEAD self-host/changelog and fresh-clone strict health will run before the single combined push; final-head CI results will be linked in the PR body. Release stays disabled and all review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-10-19T03:52:43.933Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3: reproduce the mid-file resolution false dispute caused by unrelated EOF newline state, fix the mapped-hunk comparison, and sweep conflicts/rewrite for the same assumption. Preserve genuine EOF disagreements; prove each behavior with a narrow source revert, then rerun both unchanged release gates and exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-19T03:54:34.796Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 proof: engine/conflicts.ts:253-256 now compares each mapped hunk endpoint with that side line count before reading its EOF newline; interior hunks use their inherent line boundary. New equal-middle-hunk regression runs 8 real histories (add/remove EOF newline, either resolver, recorded/legacy mode). Before/fix-only revert: 0/1, exit 1, false resolution_conflict; restored: 1/1, and genuine EOF-choice control 1/1. Linked pm test runs node --test test/resolution-propagation.test.ts: 28/28, no skips/cancellations. Sweep: conflicts resolvePayload checks rightmost range reaches EOF; competingResolutions result metadata checks mapped result endpoint; rewrite mergePath records endings only for the last aligned region (mergeContent callback). Append-only PM history newline checks concern whole event prefixes, not hunk origin. No further instances of this assumption found in either requested file. ARCHITECTURE.md documents the boundary."
  "2026-10-19T04:29:33.556Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 validation at source 39fe0f505b4122cab3895c3dc748dc9f5969633e: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check both pass 1663/1663, zero fail/skip/cancel/TODO, independent full-history clones with fresh HOME and Git global/system identity disabled. c8 --all --100 --per-file: all 67 production files, all four dimensions 100%; 23455 statements/lines, 804 functions; branches npm 7353/7353 and Bun 7351/7351. ESLint zero warnings, jscpd zero pairs/0% on 23451 lines, docstrings 67 files/365 declarations. Native TOON, real installed-CLI stat-cache strace, committed self-host, production/identity audits, package dry run, changelog, release-date and attestation checks pass. New regression plus genuine EOF and resolve/annotate controls pass in both full gates. Fresh no-local clone strict health with required merge drivers passes with only existing advisories. Final receipt commit changes only this tracker pair and the staged-source archive; runtime/tests/docs/dependencies/workflows remain identical to gated source. Claim released without closing; exact pushed-head CI will be checked on PR 125. No new CLI/SDK defect; context stale-snapshot advisory rebuilt successfully during orientation."
  "2026-10-19T04:55:11.447Z",codex-agent,"Round 4: audit resolution_conflict callers and every typed engine refusal naming a flag against the real command schemas. Add per-operation message regressions with narrow revert controls, keep the established atomic refusal behavior, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates, regenerate staged-source self-host receipts, push and wait for exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-19T04:59:23.220Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6tyfB6 fixed: engine/repo.ts supplies the invoking merge/rebase/cherry-pick/revert operation to RewriteContext; engine/rewrite.ts keeps typed resolution_conflict and atomic refusal, names pm vcs merge with its supported --record-conflicts, and names each replay operation with reconcile-first/retry guidance. These replay commands have no --continue in the actual schema. Four regressions each cover fields and text; every emitted flag is checked against the real SDK-registered command contract, plus a flag-free planner-only fallback. Reverting only the new remedy block: 0/4, exit 1 (unsupported --record-conflicts on each replay; missing explicit merge command). Restored: 4/4. Linked resolve acceptance: 32/32, no skips/cancellations."
  "2026-10-19T04:59:24.430Z",codex-agent,"Sweep evidence: inspected every engine runtime flag spelling using rg plus TypeScript AST error-constructor inventory, including indirect transport recovery strings and served error envelopes. All nine remedy flags exist on their explicitly named recovery command: authority --regenerate-legacy; merge --record-conflicts/--continue/--abort; branch --remotes; push --force; serve --auth/--root; resolve --value. Actual SDK command contracts verify all six groups. Additional ambiguity fixed at engine/serve.ts:235: read-only write refusals reach push clients, so the --auth remedy now explicitly names the operator command pm vcs serve. A real HTTP test checks push/upload/publish response messages and HttpTransport propagation against the registered serve flags. Restore only the previous error-envelope message: 0/1 exit 1; fixed: 1/1. Linked PM tests run both commands successfully (32/32 and 1/1). No further mismatch found; ARCHITECTURE.md records operation-specific recovery. Latest registry CLI is 2026.10.19; repository pin remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T05:22:38.494Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 final local gates at source 14e671761eefc7412fea0a10320f0ea82a303555: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check both pass 1667/1667 with zero fail/skip/cancel/TODO. Fresh HOME, disabled global/system Git identity and independent full-history clones. All 67 production files have c8 --all --100 --per-file at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines: 23462 statements/lines, 804 functions, npm 7354/7354 branches and Bun 7356/7356. ESLint zero warnings; jscpd zero pairs/0% on 23458 lines; docstrings 67 files/365 declarations. Native TOON, real installed-CLI stat-cache strace, committed self-host, production and identity audits, package dry-run, changelog, release-date and attestation gates all pass. New operation and HTTP regressions pass in both full gates. Exact revert commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^competing resolution .* refusal\" test/resolution-propagation.test.ts (only remedy block reverted: 0/4 exit 1; fixed 4/4); node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^an unauthenticated server\" test/serve.test.ts (only read-only error-envelope message reverted: 0/1 exit 1; fixed 1/1). Linked acceptance is 32/32 plus 1/1. Fresh no-local clone strict health with required merge drivers passes with existing advisories. No short-option remedy mismatch found. Final validation receipt changes only this tracker pair and regenerated archive; runtime/tests/docs/dependencies/workflows are identical to the gated source. Claim released without closing; pushed-head CI results will be linked on PR 125. No new PM CLI/SDK defect."
  "2026-10-21T18:54:54.067Z",codex-agent,"Tracker reconciliation authorized for the audited verdict FIXED-STALE. Re-verified unchanged main 27e1d84671fa: delivery 7609e6c61980 remains in main ancestry; engine/annotate.ts, test/edges.test.ts remain present. Resolve conflicts and propagate resolutions through automatic descendant rebase. [PR #125](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/125) (7609e6c) resolves ancestor conflict choices and propagates them through descendant native rebases. Scope: tracker state only; no new runtime certification or deployment claim."
